"Two Minutes" - Manchester United 2-1 Bayern Munich, Champions League final, Camp Nou, 26 May 1999: an animated fan retelling for the Foot All FC channel. Comic History Cartoon style (lemo-opuscar).
Unofficial: not made or endorsed by Manchester United, FC Bayern Munich, UEFA or any broadcaster. No club crests, league or
competition marks, broadcast footage or real likenesses are used; players are generic paper puppets identified by shirt number,
the trophy is a generic drawn cup.

Puppet art: the part sheets of videos/barca-remontada-short (ChatGPT image model in Figma, gpt-image-2.5-flare, AI-generated),
  recoloured into plain kits with tools/recolor_kit.py (plain red 'utd', generic white 'opp').
Narration: Microsoft VibeVoice-Realtime-0.5B, voice "Frank" (MIT licence), AI-generated voice.
Fonts (SIL Open Font License): IM FELL English SC (Igino Marini), Old Standard TT (Alexey Kryukov), Lilita One (Juan Montoreano).
Instruments (sampled, via lemo-opuscar core/audio/sampler.py): see out/instruments.txt at build time.
Samples (CC0): FreePats project (freepats.zenvoid.org), VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition (Versilian Studios), Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios)
Foley, crowd and applause: synthesized in mix.py.
Facts: see social/scripts/man-utd-1999-final.md (fact sheet with sources).
